# Version and documents

Every change to this project bumps the version and updates the records below. Do this in the same change, not as a follow-up.

1. In `src/product/releases.ts`, set `APP_VERSION` and prepend a release. Use the next patch for a correction, the next minor for a new capability. Each release lists what changed, in sentences a reader of the page can understand.
2. Set the version line at the top of `docs/vision-and-requirements.md` and `docs/architecture-and-design.md` to that same version.
3. If goals, scope, or requirements changed, edit the vision document. If structure, walks, diagrams, or decisions changed, edit the architecture document, including the conceptual, logical, or physical diagram that the change affects.
4. Add the same version and changes under Version history in both documents.
5. If the on-page summary would be wrong after the change, update `src/product/summary.ts`.

The version shown on the page is `APP_VERSION`. Do not leave the documents on an older version than the app.
